  "verbalization": "Abrotanifolon is implicated in the interaction with Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular pathways, with the target entity consistently identified as VMRC-LCP in all three paths. This suggests that Abrotanifolon acts as a modulator of VMRC-LCP, which in turn targets Neuropilin-2. The shared target of VMRC-LCP across different compounds indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the regulation of Neuropilin-2 through the VMRC-LCP pathway. The evidence from the three paths supports a hierarchical relationship where Abrotanifolon influences VMRC-LCP, which then affects Neuropilin-2. The consistency in the target relationships across the paths strengthens the hypothesis that Abrotanifolon exerts its biological effect via this specific pathway, highlighting the importance of VMRC-LCP in mediating the interaction with Neuropilin-2.",
